- Approved r12 identifiers: works.relux.tunnel.mac and works.relux.tunnel.mac.tunnel; macOS 15 minimum.
- Target-owned plists, Development and Developer ID entitlement files, App Group/Keychain absence, exact system-extension embedding, and shared protocol/build version.
- Provider imports NetworkExtension and exposes only empty start/stop plus version-message handling; no packet, route, DNS, HEV, SSH, or relay implementation.
- Swift Testing contract suites cover identity/profile values, bundle relationship, deployment floor, plist values, entitlement contents, minimal lifecycle, and version compatibility. The existing ReluxProxy SwiftPM executable remains separate.

## Passing evidence (real exit codes)

- make macos-targets-validate: 0. Generates from checked-in inputs, builds Debug and Release credential-free, runs 5 host plus 4 provider tests, and inspects the built app for exactly one embedded provider, exact identifiers, matching versions, macOS 15 floor, and provider class.
- make workspace-validate: 0. Two clean generations are deterministic and the six existing schemes remain present.
- swift test: 0. 443 tests in 37 suites passed with 25 pre-existing declared known issues.
- swift format lint --strict --recursive App Tests Sources Project.swift Package.swift: 0.
- tuist inspect implicit-imports: 0.
- plist lint, shell syntax, executable-mode, git diff --check, and task-board validate: 0.

## Gate P0 Stop-The-Line evidence

Three signed build strategies were attempted without editing generated Xcode state; each exited 65. Manual signing proves the installed host profile Mac Team Provisioning Profile: works.relux.tunnel.mac lacks the System Extension capability and com.apple.developer.system-extension.install. Automatic refresh reports no usable Xcode account credentials. A provider-only automatic lane selected an Apple Development identity and reached CodeSign, then failed errSecInternalComponent, showing the private key is inaccessible to this non-interactive session. The installed provider profile does contain packet-tunnel-provider; no installed profile contains system-extension.install.

Exact external input required: a human with team 262RZ595FP access must enable/confirm System Extension for works.relux.tunnel.mac, regenerate/install its macOS development profile, restore a usable Xcode account session and Apple Development private-key access, then rerun the signed ReluxProxyMac Debug build. Entitlements were not weakened.

## Important anomaly

Linking the out-of-scope live ReluxTunnelMacOSAdapter exposed an existing Xcode ProcessXCFramework output collision between ReluxLibSSH2 and CReluxNativeFixture at include/module.modulemap. The compile-only provider therefore correctly links only ReluxTunnelCore; the later runtime-integration task must resolve the packaging collision before adding transport composition.

